Nah. But the Yankees concluded their two-city, three-opponent road trip Wednesday night with a temporarily characteristic win, putting together 11 singles, two walks, a stolen base and one double to outlast the Cardinals, 7-4, at Busch Stadium and secure a 5-4 record on this Midwest swing.
