And to give starting pitcher Hiroki Kuroda even more breathing room, the Yankees came right back in the fourth with a Johnson leadoff single and, following two straight outs, a Roberts double, an Ellsbury two-run single and a shift-beating single into short right field by McCann that scored Ellsbury after he stole second base unchallenged.
The Yankees exhibited a fundamentals clinic, as they did for all of their victories on this trip. For the night, they went 4-for-9 and drew a walk with runners in scoring position. In their five wins over the Cubs, White Sox and Cardinals, they went 16-for-42 (.381) with a walk in these clutch situations.
